-- Capabilities widening, Task 2 -- Check 4 (transitive `use`), the ACCEPT
-- side. `Vault` (`stdlib/vault.march:26`) declares `needs IO.Mut`. Any module
-- that `use`s `Vault` inherits an obligation to cover `IO.Mut` too --
-- `check_module_needs`'s Check 4 (`typecheck.ml:5661`) walks every `DUse`,
-- looks up the imported module's own declared-needs in `env.module_caps`
-- (populated when the imported module finished checking, `typecheck.ml:7012`,
-- `(name.txt, inner_needs) :: env'.module_caps`), and requires each of THOSE
-- caps to be covered -- via the same `cap_subsumes` subsumption Check 1 uses
-- -- by the IMPORTING module's own `needs`. Here `Main` declares `needs
-- IO.Mut` itself, so the transitive obligation from `use Vault` is satisfied
-- (`cap_subsumes "IO.Mut" "IO.Mut"` holds reflexively). See reject/t39 for
-- the same shape with the `needs IO.Mut` line removed. See
-- core-march-types.md §2.8.6.
mod Main do
  needs IO.Mut
  use Vault

  fn main() do
    ()
  end
end
